  "_id": "tg-rebellion",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "they will not believe me, nor hearken, Ex. 4:1. murmured against Moses and Aaron, Ex. 16:2. rebel not ye against the Lord, Num. 14:9. ye rebelled against my word at … Meribah, Num. 20:24. ye rebelled against my commandment in the desert, Num. 27:14. ye … rebelled against the commandment, Deut. 1:26 (1:43). Ye have been rebellious, Deut. 9:24. I know thy rebellion, Deut. 31:27. Whosoever … doth rebel … shall be put to death, Josh. 1:18. not rebel against the commandment, 1 Sam. 12:14. rebellion is as the sin of witchcraft, 1 Sam. 15:23. Israel rebelled against the house of David, 1 Kgs. 12:19 (2 Chr. 10:19). Zedekiah rebelled against the king of Babylon, 2 Kgs. 24:20 (2 Chr. 36:13; Jer. 52:3). rebellion and sedition have been made therein, Ezra 4:19. in their rebellion appointed a captain to return, Neh. 9:17. disobedient, and rebelled against thee, Neh. 9:26. rebellious dwell in a dry land, Ps. 68:6. rebelled against the words of God, Ps. 107:11. evil man seeketh only rebellion, Prov. 17:11. ye will revolt more and more, Isa. 1:5. if ye refuse and rebel, Isa. 1:20. regard not the work of the Lord, Isa. 5:12 (2 Ne. 15:12). people turneth not unto him, Isa. 9:13 (2 Ne. 19:13). Woe to the rebellious children, Isa. 30:1. they rebelled, and vexed his holy Spirit, Isa. 63:10. this people hath … a rebellious heart, Jer. 5:23. send thee to … Israel … a rebellious nation, Ezek. 2:3. Notwithstanding the children rebelled, Ezek. 20:21. I will purge out … the rebels, Ezek. 20:38. though we have rebelled against him, Dan. 9:9. they do not return to the Lord their God, Hosea 7:10.",
